  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "claim": "The diff adds administrator removal of disabled projects, a persistent removal marker, current-project filtering and a console action. The Go module selects a patched Gorilla WebSocket revision and its proxy dependency. The source of the version and health commands, health and metrics handlers, and protocol error handlers is unchanged.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "1e16e117525a756c301873d22685fbc0bd20f37e",
        "method": "Reviewed git diff --name-status --find-renames from c779976b4b4e95cda9d10a7a19649de6c6ec1bfd to the reviewed commit. Its 34 product paths include the renamed console asset, embedded index, Access, Requests and UsageQuotas pages and their tests. The pinned review CLI lists 27 changed paths and stops at the old asset name. The Git diff supplied the remaining paths. The reviewed source digest covers the complete tracked product tree."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "claim": "A disposable database produced by the prior binary at schema 26 upgraded to schema 27. After project removal and gateway restart the removed slug stayed reserved, its recorded usage retained its project and key identity, and the surviving project could still use the shared provider connection.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/iam/schema.go, go/internal/iam/project_removal_test.go, go/internal/iam/migration_test.go",
        "method": "The candidate before the dependency update was exercised over HTTP with old and new binaries, a disposable database and local provider. After restart its management lists, attribution and surviving project were checked. The same IAM code and migration tests passed on the reviewed commit."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "claim": "The administrator endpoint rejects an active project, an unknown ID, a project credential, and non-admin or cross-origin SSO mutations. An authorized same-origin deletion succeeds. A failed audit insert returns a server error and preserves the disabled project. Retrying after recovery records its request ID. Six concurrent HTTP deletions produced one durable audit event.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/project_delete_test.go, go/internal/api/audit.go, go/internal/iam/repository.go",
        "method": "Focused HTTP tests used a disposable store and audit-insert failure. The initial candidate binary was also exercised concurrently and after restart. The reviewed commit passed the complete Go suite including the HTTP and IAM removal tests."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "claim": "All 285 console tests passed. Consecutive builds produced identical assets, and the candidate binary served the final script byte-for-byte. The console confirmation identifies the project, discloses slug reservation and explains the effect on historical usage and provider connections.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/web/console/src/pages/Access.tsx, go/internal/web/console/tests/project-page.test.mjs, go/internal/web/console/dist/index.html",
        "method": "The console suite and repeated builds exercised these assets on the project-removal candidate. The candidate binary served the generated script over HTTP. The dependency follow-up changed only go/go.mod and go/go.sum."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "claim": "The reviewed commit passed the complete uncached Go suite, build, vet and the CI-pinned static analyzer. Gateway HTTP fixtures covered key-scoped model discovery, administrator authentication, embedded console serving and default-off metrics. The project-removal candidate also passed the documentation checker and exercised model access for a surviving project.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/models_test.go, go/internal/api/sso_test.go, go/internal/api/server_test.go, go/internal/api/observe_test.go, scripts/check-docs.mjs",
        "method": "go test -count=1 ./..., go build ./..., go vet ./... and the CI-pinned staticcheck from go/. The project-removal candidate also ran node scripts/check-docs.mjs and a local binary smoke."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "claim": "The updated indirect Gorilla WebSocket package is used by the gateway realtime bridge. All four Gemini realtime API tests passed against loopback, covering a voice and tool roundtrip, route adaptation boundaries, cancellation and the advertised handshake profile. The Go vulnerability scan reported no reachable findings after the GO-2026-6278 update.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/go.mod, go/go.sum, go/internal/api/realtime_gemini.go, go/internal/api/realtime_gemini_test.go",
        "method": "go test ./internal/api -run '^TestGeminiRealtime' -count=1 on the reviewed commit. The CI-pinned govulncheck, module verification and go mod tidy -diff also completed successfully."
      }
    }
  ],
